# One line. Run from the repo root by `orgasmic verify TASK-K5NDR`.
#
# WHY THIS COMMAND SETS THE VARIABLE INSTEAD OF UNSETTING IT
#
# Every other artifact here prefixes with `env -u ORGASMIC_RUN_ID -u
# ORGASMIC_HOME` because run identity leaking into a test subprocess breaks the
# suite. This task IS that leak, so the proof needs the leak present: `verify`
# scrubs both variables from the child (`SCRUBBED_ENV` in `src/verify.rs`), and
# a replay with nothing set could never reproduce the defect. The command
# re-exports a run id of its own instead.
#
# The value is deliberately a well-formed run id that no daemon can be holding,
# so the red is the same on the operator's laptop, in a dispatch pane, and on a
# machine with no daemon at all. The natural red used the worker's REAL ambient
# id (`run-20260729T032421-3731a4fbb09f4aa78b6f43db04e70d63`) and produced the
# identical signature; pinning a live id would make the proof depend on that run
# still existing.
#
# ONE test, and the one TASK-6AYEJ measured. `dispatch finalize` is where
# `manager.rs` reads `ORGASMIC_RUN_ID` and resolves a run by it, so this is the
# shortest path from the leak to a failure. The whole `dispatch` binary would
# also go red under the injection, but a proof that fails broadly cannot show it
# reproduced the defect it names.
env ORGASMIC_RUN_ID=run-20200101T000000-k5ndrverifynotalive0000000000000 cargo test -p orgasmic-cli --test dispatch dispatch_finalize_commit_flag_leaves_clean_committed_worktree
